\exfigure{1372_q25_1}

How far, in metres, is the particle from the origin, 150 seconds later?

solutions.latex:
\exfigure{165_q8_s1}

The distance is the area under the velocity–time graph: a rectangle for the $15$ s at $4$ m/s plus two triangles with total base $35-15=20$ s:
$$\begin{aligned}A&=15\times4+\dfrac{1}{2}\times4\times(35-15)\\&=60+2\times20\\&=100\end{aligned}$$

Using period $=\dfrac{2\pi}{n}$ with $n=\dfrac{\pi}{4}$:
$$\begin{aligned}\text{Period}&=\dfrac{2\pi}{\frac{\pi}{4}}\\ &=8\end{aligned}$$
